	(footprint "cec-Connector_PinHeader_2.54mm:PinHeader_1x04_P2.54mm_Horizontal_LongPin"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "5de0d680-ce13-4b7a-9e10-c7c8bd9d6040")
		(at 46.45 19.98)
		(descr "1x4 2.54mm RIGHT-ANGLE Dupont-class pin header, LONG mating tails -- the iteration-5 24-pin daughterboard signal stub (blade-fit memo addendum 5). Authored in MOUNTED orientation: 4 THT pads along X at 2.54mm; body (~2.5mm deep) and the bent pins extend +Y, i.e. toward and PAST the daughterboard's bottom edge, pins pointing straight down parallel to the FASTON blades at the header's own ~2.5mm face standoff (the bend line), blind-mating a vertical 1x4 female socket on the main board in the same single drop as the blade set. MATING-LENGTH REQUIREMENT (why LONG-tail): at the recomputed uniform 12.4mm bottom-edge float and an ~8.5mm-tall Dupont female, a standard ~6mm tail leaves the pin tip ~2mm ABOVE the socket entry -- zero engagement; tails must reach >=2.5-3mm into the contact zone => below-edge pin length >= ~7mm engaged / 10-12mm class preferred (commodity 'long-pin'/stacking 2.54 headers run 10-15mm). LCSC carries the generic RA 2.54 header class (Ckmtw/Cankemeng lines); the specific long-pin MPN is pinned at the OQ-89 SKU pass -- consigned acceptable. Pads 1.7mm/drill 1.0 (KiCad convention). Pin 1 = leftmost (square silk tick).")
